  "review_corrections_before_acceptance": [
    "New typed draft initially derived list request indices from unavailable-name ordering. Independent review identified the mismatch with Source multivalue metadata order. Private Slot.collection_index now captures the actual Source index, or dense derived output position. Different-type and same-type providers, explicit/wildcard/derived reorder, and metadata drift all pass without changing answer goldens.",
    "List aliases remain registered as unreferenceable/unstable entries rather than disappearing from alias lookup. Duplicate list/scalar aliases remain AmbiguousName; no list placeholder enters the scalar frame. Scalar aliases and scalar/positional ORDER BY after interleaved lists use dense scalar indices.",
    "Stored list copying has its own metered IEEE-preserving branch. Ordinary Runtime.copy and scalar .Value nonfinite refusals remain unchanged. Typed Single/Double lists retain signed zero, subnormal, infinity and signed NaN payload bits through derived copies.",
    "The schema-discovery wrapper retains its existing phase contract: authorized scalar dependency discovery may occur before full typed admission. The dynamic pivot/join test proves Unsupported with no result and zero collection scans after scalar discovery; no blanket pre-scan claim is made for this wrapper."
  ],
  "contracts": [
    "QueryValue is a query-result enum, separate from core Value/ExpressionValue and scalar evaluator operands. Complete MultivalueValue lists retain order, duplicates, NULL children and empty lists without display conversion.",
    "Explicit Multivalue output metadata carries an element TypeDescriptor and child nullability. Missing-parent/NULL-list association and SQL collection equality are not invented.",
    "Row-local SELECT, wildcards, AS names, static named/derived chains, scalar WHERE/ORDER BY and TOP work. A direct hidden .Value criterion selects parents while the selected bare field retains its full list.",
    "Whole typed plan admission and leaf metadata checks precede collection scans. Scalar/expression/progressive APIs cannot publish list outputs; unsupported typed list joins/UNION/DISTINCT/keys/aggregates/crosstabs/mixed visible .Value plans do not enter collection cursors.",
    "Every requested stored child is validated, including suffixes after matching criteria. Source visitor failures are sticky and no failed prefix becomes a query result or complete source cache.",
    "Separate scalar frames and indexed list sidecars preserve scalar alias positions, owner/depth restoration and immutable bindings. No list IDs or NULL sentinels are fed to scalar kernels.",
    "All new buffers/payload copies use fallible paid allocation, shared query byte/row/work limits and cancellation. Repeated/derived child copies consume additional cumulative resources. Scalar-only collection API results use the ordinary evaluator and paid typed publication.",
    "Three isolated requested one-MiB stack probes prove 50 static named typed sources succeed and 51 refuses before scans; five inline layers use existing selected depth32, while default16 and the absolute32 guard retain checked refusals. These are engineering proofs, not native Access depth qualification."
  ],
